  "term": "gated channel",
  "definition": "A gated channel is a model component used in a gated channel-spatial attention mechanism to regulate how channel-based information is emphasized during processing. In the source, it is part of a hybrid network designed to improve discriminative feature learning and more efficient feature integration.",
